--  Ending a session with a status a caller can read.
--
--  Adash's command language is Ada, so a script is Ada statements and the
--  internal commands are called the way Ada calls a procedure -- with
--  parentheses and a semicolon, not with bare words. That is the whole point
--  of the language choice, and it is the first thing a reader has to see.

quit (3);
